  "body": "## Problem\n\nPR #2192 (#2181) keeps a full copy of the cut layer for each playback keyframe. On the dense face fixture 68 keyframes use 424 MiB of the 512 MiB budget. A larger program gets a larger stride, so a jump cuts more moves.\n\n## Proposal\n\nShare the field bricks that did not change between two keyframes (copy-on-write, for example `Arc` bricks in the simulation crate). Then the same budget holds more keyframes.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test: the keyframe bytes of the dense face fall by a stated factor.\n- The replay stays bit-identical to the live cut at each move.\n- The stock simulation verdict and the post gate stay unchanged.\n\nFollow-up of #2181.\n",
